, copper, carbon steel, stainless steel, titanium, and other specialty steel products; and provides metals processing services to consumer products, general manufacturing, non-residential construction, transportation, aerospace, energy, electronics and semiconductor fabrication, industrial machinery, and heavy industries. It sells its products directly to original equipment manufacturers, which primarily include small machine shops and fabricators. The company was formerly known as Reliance Steel & Aluminum Co. and changed its name to Reliance, Inc. in February 2024. Reliance, Inc. was founded in 1939 and is based in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Karla R. Lewis CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 15K people. Revenue per employee of $910K ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $32K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Reliance, Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $20.3B market cap on $14.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $502M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 18\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 65% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6523472580871983},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $9.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Basic Materials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 15% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","31 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Is Reliance (RS) Down 0.7% Since Last Earnings Report?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3033307/why-is-reliance-rs-down-0-7-since-last-earnings-report?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3033307","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795188610.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"How Did Firmer Steel Pricing Lift Results at Reliance (NYSE:RS) Now?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/metal-and-mining/how-did-firmer-steel-pricing-lift-results-at-reliance-nysers-now-1","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795166760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(RS) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/RS_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_111926104402_1795103042.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795103042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reliance Inc's Dividend Analysis","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/reliance-incs-dividend-analysis-100452196.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795169092.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"BASFY Partners With DWE to Advance Renewable Methanol Production","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3033244/basfy-partners-with-dwe-to-advance-renewable-methanol-production?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_corporate_actions-3033244","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795185900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why You Should Hold Onto Sherwin-Williams Stock for Now","source":"zacks.com"